  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as a する verb: {起訴|きそ}する (to indict, to prosecute). The passive {起訴|きそ}される (to be indicted) is very common in news reporting.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {起訴|きそ}する: to indict, to prosecute\n- {不起訴|ふきそ}: non-indictment, decision not to prosecute\n- {起訴|きそ}{猶予|ゆうよ}: suspended indictment\n- {起訴|きそ}{状|じょう}: indictment document\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nJapan's conviction rate after indictment exceeds 99%, so prosecutors are very selective about which cases they bring to trial. The decision to indict or not ({不起訴|ふきそ}) is itself a major news event.",
